    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "15. Stratagems",
    "ruleNumber": "15.09",
    "order": 200,
    "anchor": "15.09",
    "summary": "A unit uses Snap Shooting (15.09) only as the rule that grants it allows. The unit shoots following [Making Attacks](vsdata:core-rule/making-attacks) (04), with these limits:\n\n- it can target just one enemy unit, which must be an eligible target, [visible](vsdata:core-rule/visibility) and up to 24\" from it\n- each attack hits only if its [Hit roll](vsdata:core-rule/hit-rolls) is an unmodified 6, whatever the weapon's BS or any modifiers\n- Hit rolls can't be re-rolled\n\nThe unit can't start an [action](vsdata:core-rule/actions) for the rest of the phase.",
